        </table>
      </note>
      <!-- Accordion 1 End -->
      <!-- Accordion 2: Lesson Level -->
      <note id="note-00017">
        <title>Lesson Level</title>
                  <para id="para-00100"> Applicable information is dispersed
        throughout the student pages at the lesson level so they are intermittently reminded of how
        the Algebra 1 content plays a part in our lives. </para>
          <para id="para-00101"> The following
        sample appears at the end of Activity 2.9.2: Graphing Inequalities. Notice how it ties the
        algebra content from this specific lesson to the overall “Why Should I Care?” topic for the
        unit. </para>
          <para id="para-00102">
          <media alt="A screenshot from the student curriculum showing one of the embedded Why Should I Care elements. The content focus in these sections is about creating relevance and this example explains how a food entrepreneur uses linear inequalities. The provided image is a bowl containing a variety of fruit.">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_12_02_01_12.png"/>
          </media>

        </para>
      </note>
      <!-- Accordion 2 End -->
